
APPLE LISA UNIX -- SYSTEM V

Here is your Unix software. It is Bell Labs Unix System V.

The Unix manuals are very well written and comprehensive: they can
answer almost all your questions. Be sure to review the 
"See also" sections mentioned at the bottom of the manual pages, since
many of the commands refer to other commands.

We have made a directory called /usr/unix.info

In that directory are a number of files which describe Unix features
of general interest. We have tried to anticipate common user questions
to make Unix easier for you to use and configure. Please look at those files.


NOTE TO USERS WHO HAVE BEEN SHIPPED UNIX ON DISKS LARGER THAN 20-MEG:

	We have placed the "system" onto /dev/c4a, and have made
	another filesystem, /dev/c4c. You should put your work
	onto /dev/c4c.

	To access the other filesystem:

		mount /dev/c4c /t
		cd /t
		.
		.
		.

	Also, you should edit the file /etc/checklist, and
	add /dev/c4c to the list.

NOTE TO ALL USERS:

UNIX SYSTEMS SHOULD BE "SYNC"ED TWICE PRIOR TO SHUTDOWN.
ALSO, PLEASE RUN THE FSCK PROGRAM FREQUENTLY.

	ex: fsck /dev/c4a


